From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] icu: UText and regular expressions

Windows Terminal gives its text buffer to ICU as a UText and searches it with ICU's regular expressions (URL detection on every repaint, the search box); icu.dll had neither, and the missing utext_setup ended every repaint. icu.dll now has ICU's UText (utext_setup, utext_close, utext_nativeLength; the public 144-byte layout) and a regular expression engine of our own behind the uregex API Windows Terminal and others use (open, clone, close, setText, setUText, find, find64, findNext, matches, reset, start/end and their 64-bit forms, groupCount, pattern, flags, time and stack limits): literals and escapes, ., classes with ranges and \d \w \s, \b \B ^ $ \A \z \Z, groups, alternation, greedy and lazy quantifiers and intervals, and the CASE_INSENSITIVE, MULTILINE, DOTALL, LITERAL and COMMENTS flags, matched with a backtracking machine over the provider's chunks.
---
